<LegalLayout title="Privacy Policy" heading="How your info gets handled here." lastUpdated="May 2026">
  <p>
    This is the privacy policy for <strong>westondeanmusic.com</strong>. It covers what the site collects, what happens to it, and how to reach me if you have questions.
  </p>

  <h2>Short version</h2>
  <p>
    This site is a one-page marketing page for a solo musician. It doesn't have user accounts, doesn't sell anything, and doesn't run third-party trackers. The only ways you can share information with me through it are by clicking the email link, the phone link, or by booking through The Stage Finder.
  </p>

  <h2>What this site collects</h2>
  <p>
    On its own, almost nothing. The site is a static page hosted on Cloudflare Pages. Cloudflare's edge network sees your IP address and basic request data the way any web server does. Cloudflare may keep that briefly for security and analytics purposes under its own privacy policies.
  </p>
  <p>
    If I have Cloudflare Web Analytics turned on for the site, it counts page views without using cookies or tracking individuals. There's no Google Analytics, Facebook Pixel, or similar.
  </p>

  <h2>What happens when you contact me</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Email link:</strong> tapping the booking email opens your email app with a draft addressed to me. The message goes through your email provider and mine. I keep booking inquiries long enough to answer them and run the gig.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Phone link:</strong> tapping the number dials me. Standard call records apply, nothing special.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Stage Finder:</strong> clicking any "Book on The Stage Finder" or "See available dates" link takes you off this site to thestagefinder.com. Anything you do there is covered by{' '}
      <a href="https://thestagefinder.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">The Stage Finder's privacy policy</a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Social links:</strong> Instagram and TikTok links go to those platforms, which have their own privacy practices.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What I do with what you share</h2>
  <p>
    Use it to answer you, talk through the gig, and confirm the date. I don't sell, rent, or hand it to anyone else. I don't add you to a mailing list (there isn't one).
  </p>

  <h2>Your choices</h2>
  <p>
    You can decline to contact me, and the site won't know the difference. If you've emailed me and want me to delete what we exchanged, ask and I will.
  </p>

  <h2>Kids</h2>
  <p>
    This site isn't aimed at children under 13. Booking is for venues and event hosts. If you think a child sent me a booking inquiry, let me know and I'll delete it.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    If this policy changes meaningfully, the date at the top updates. The substance is unlikely to change much, since the site does so little.
  </p>

  <h2>Questions</h2>
  <p>
    Email <a href="mailto:booking@westondeanmusic.com">booking@westondeanmusic.com</a> with the subject "privacy" and I'll get back to you.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
